# 📱 MeroPrize PWA Implementation Plan

This document outlines the step-by-step plan to transform **MeroPrize** into a full-featured, installable **Progressive Web App (PWA)** compatible with **iOS (Safari)**, **Android (Chrome)**, and **Desktop (Edge/Chrome)**.

---

## 🎯 PWA Objectives

1. **Instant Installability**: Users can tap "Add to Home Screen" or "Install App" on mobile and desktop without going through an app store.
2. **Offline Mode & Caching**: Access saved coupons, draw dates, and offline fallback views even without an active internet connection.
3. **App-Like Feel**: Standalone window without browser address bars, smooth page transitions, and native splash screens.
4. **Push Notifications (Phase 2)**: Notify users when new IRD draw results are published or when a saved coupon wins.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture & Component Breakdown

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Browser / Mobile Client] -->|Reads| B[Web App Manifest / manifest.json]
    A -->|Registers| C[Service Worker / sw.js]
    A -->|Prompts| D[PWA Install Banner / PwaInstallPrompt]
    C -->|Caches| E[Static Shell: CSS, Fonts, Images]
    C -->|Network First / Cache Fallback| F[Dashboard API / Coupons Data]
    C -->|Offline Fallback| G[Offline Screen: /offline]
```

---

## 📋 Step-by-Step Implementation Strategy

### Step 1: Icon Generation & Public Assets
Generate high-resolution PNG icon variants with proper padding and maskable backgrounds.

| Asset | Size / Format | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `public/icons/icon-192.png` | 192x192 PNG | Standard Android Home Screen icon |
| `public/icons/icon-512.png` | 512x512 PNG | High-DPI Android Home Screen / Splash icon |
| `public/icons/maskable-512.png` | 512x512 PNG | Adaptive Android maskable icon |
| `public/icons/apple-touch-icon.png` | 180x180 PNG | iOS Safari home screen icon |
| `public/favicon.ico` | 32x32 ICO | Browser tab icon |

---

### Step 2: Dynamic Web App Manifest (`app/manifest.ts`)
Implement Next.js App Router dynamic manifest file to ensure accurate manifest metadata and shortcut links.

```typescript
import { MetadataRoute } from 'next';

export default function manifest(): MetadataRoute.Manifest {
  return {
    name: 'MeroPrize — Pay Bill • Win Everyday',
    short_name: 'MeroPrize',
    description: 'Save IRD coupons once and check them automatically against official winner lists.',
    start_url: '/dashboard',
    display: 'standalone',
    orientation: 'portrait',
    background_color: '#14161C',
    theme_color: '#16181F',
    categories: ['utilities', 'finance', 'lifestyle'],
    icons: [
      {
        src: '/icons/icon-192.png',
        sizes: '192x192',
        type: 'image/png',
        purpose: 'any',
      },
      {
        src: '/icons/icon-512.png',
        sizes: '512x512',
        type: 'image/png',
        purpose: 'any',
      },
      {
        src: '/icons/maskable-512.png',
        sizes: '512x512',
        type: 'image/png',
        purpose: 'maskable',
      },
    ],
    shortcuts: [
      {
        name: 'My Coupons',
        short_name: 'Coupons',
        url: '/dashboard/coupons',
        icons: [{ src: '/icons/icon-192.png', sizes: '192x192' }],
      },
      {
        name: 'IRD Draws',
        short_name: 'Draws',
        url: '/dashboard/draws',
        icons: [{ src: '/icons/icon-192.png', sizes: '192x192' }],
      },
    ],
  };
}
```

---

### Step 3: Service Worker & Caching Engine (`public/sw.js`)
Create a lightweight, robust custom Service Worker for offline support and static asset caching.

- **Pre-Cache Static Shell**: Cache `/`, `/dashboard`, `/offline`, logo assets, and CSS.
- **Network-First for Dynamic Routes**: Fetch latest dashboard data from server; if network fails, load cached state.
- **Offline Page Fallback**: Display a clean "You are offline" screen if navigating to uncached pages.

```javascript
// public/sw.js
const CACHE_NAME = 'meroprize-cache-v1';
const STATIC_ASSETS = [
  '/',
  '/dashboard',
  '/offline',
  '/trophy-icon.png',
  '/logo.png',
  '/manifest.json'
];

self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.open(CACHE_NAME).then((cache) => cache.addAll(STATIC_ASSETS))
  );
  self.skipWaiting();
});

self.addEventListener('activate', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.keys().then((keys) =>
      Promise.all(keys.map((k) => k !== CACHE_NAME && caches.delete(k)))
    )
  );
  self.clients.claim();
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  if (event.request.mode === 'navigate') {
    event.respondWith(
      fetch(event.request).catch(() => caches.match(event.request) || caches.match('/offline'))
    );
  }
});
```

---

### Step 4: Service Worker Registration & Meta Tags (`app/layout.tsx`)
Add standard PWA viewport meta tags and register the Service Worker on window load.

- `apple-mobile-web-app-capable: yes`
- `apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style: black-translucent`
- Service Worker registration script in layout.

---

### Step 5: Native "Install MeroPrize App" Prompt (`PwaInstallPrompt.tsx`)
Create a user-friendly UI banner inside the dashboard that:
1. Listens for the browser's `beforeinstallprompt` event (Android / Chrome).
2. Displays an "Install MeroPrize App" button with app icon.
3. Detects iOS Safari and provides step-by-step instructions (*Tap Share → Add to Home Screen*).

---

### Step 6: Offline Screen (`app/offline/page.tsx`)
A styled offline screen matching MeroPrize design guidelines, allowing users to retry connection or view cached coupons.

---

## 🚦 Execution Order & Milestones

| Milestone | Tasks | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :---: |
| **Milestone 1** | Generate crisp 192px, 512px, Maskable, Apple Touch icons | ⏳ Ready to build |
| **Milestone 2** | Add dynamic `app/manifest.ts` & update `app/layout.tsx` metadata | ⏳ Ready to build |
| **Milestone 3** | Create `public/sw.js` Service Worker & Register in root layout | ⏳ Ready to build |
| **Milestone 4** | Build `PwaInstallPrompt.tsx` banner & `/offline` fallback page | ⏳ Ready to build |
| **Milestone 5** | Verify PWA Lighthouse score (100/100 PWA audit) | ⏳ Ready to build |

---

> [!TIP]
> Once Milestone 1–4 are executed, users will see the native **"Install App"** prompt when opening MeroPrize on mobile devices or Chrome!
